    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1546">

                <pb facs="1678" n="1664" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg1664"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">831.6363/1642: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Venezuela</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-29T19:00:00-04:30">April 29, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 30—1:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>460. I again conferred with British and Netherlands Ministers today and concerted
                    plans for preliminary memoranda to Venezuelan <pb facs="1679" n="1665"
                        xml:id="pg1665"/> Government to be presented separately by each [to] Foreign
                        Minister<anchor n="52" xml:id="d1546-f1"/> next week.</p>
                <p>Communications to be presented are in substantial agreement, but that of
                    Netherlands Minister will particularly stress point of discriminatory treatment
                    as applied to Dutch possessions.</p>
                <p>My memorandum will follow lines of Department’s 377, April 28, 8 p.m., stressing
                    reasons presented in numbered paragraph 3 of Department’s 367, April 26, but
                    with introductory phrase to second paragraph: “aside from considerations related
                    to successful pursuance of the war effort and continental defense”, in deference
                    to British desire not to omit mention of this point.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1546-f1" n="52" xml:id="d1546-f1-content">
